WEBVTT

1
00:00:25.833 --> 00:00:30.000


2
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.833
<b>Here, Lord Krishna presents a summary of</b>
<b>his previous teachings. </b>

3
00:00:35.833 --> 00:00:37.166
<b>He says,</b>

4
00:00:37.166 --> 00:00:38.208
<b>"Arjuna, </b>

5
00:00:38.208 --> 00:00:41.875
<b>if you meet your death in this battle,</b>

6
00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:44.083
<b>you shall attain heaven,</b>

7
00:00:44.083 --> 00:00:48.708
<b>and if you emerge victorious, </b>
<b>you shall rule over the entire earth. </b>

8
00:00:48.708 --> 00:00:50.125
<b>Therefore, arise </b>

9
00:00:50.125 --> 00:00:51.541
<b>and fight."</b>

10
00:00:56.458 --> 00:01:03.375
<b>When we're traveling on a road, </b>
<b>we typically face just two choices </b>

11
00:01:03.375 --> 00:01:05.250
<b>we either turn left</b>

12
00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:06.541
<b>or right. </b>

13
00:01:06.541 --> 00:01:08.375
<b>How simple is that!</b>

14
00:01:08.375 --> 00:01:13.625
<b>Krishna presents Arjuna's choices with </b>
<b>the same simplicity. </b>

15
00:01:13.625 --> 00:01:15.250
<b>There are only two paths</b>

16
00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:16.750
<b>to fight</b>

17
00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:18.875
<b>or not to fight. </b>

18
00:01:18.875 --> 00:01:21.750
<b>If you fight and lose</b>

19
00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:28.166
<b>you'll attain heaven for your efforts in </b>
<b>establishing dharma and fulfilling your duty.</b>

20
00:01:28.166 --> 00:01:30.791
<b>If you fight and win</b>

21
00:01:30.791 --> 00:01:37.500
<b>righteousness prevails, adharma is defeated, </b>
<b>and you gain dominion over the entire earth.</b>

22
00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.500
<b>If you don't fight at all</b>

23
00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:47.541
<b>you'll only earn dishonor, along with the sin of </b>
<b>failing your dharma and duty.</b>

24
00:01:47.541 --> 00:01:55.125
<b>Besides, it's not even certain that those whose </b>
<b>death Arjuna fears will actually die in this war.</b>

25
00:01:55.125 --> 00:02:01.458
<b>Whether Arjuna fights or not, </b>
<b>the war will happen anyway.</b>

26
00:02:01.458 --> 00:02:06.666
<b>The conclusion is remarkably simple </b>
<b>fighting is indeed the right choice!</b>

27
00:02:11.625 --> 00:02:15.625
<b>Every choice carries its own consequences.</b>

28
00:02:15.625 --> 00:02:23.291
<b>The decision to choose any path</b>
<b>isn't inherently right or wrong</b>

29
00:02:23.291 --> 00:02:31.750
<b>but the outcomes of that choice </b>
<b>can certainly be good or bad.</b>

30
00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:37.833
<b>So how should one make decisions?</b>

31
00:02:37.833 --> 00:02:43.208
<b>Some people make choices swept away</b>
<b> by momentary emotions.</b>

32
00:02:43.208 --> 00:02:46.208
<b>This is exactly what Arjuna is doing now,</b>

33
00:02:46.208 --> 00:02:52.291
<b>overwhelmed by his feelings for his loved ones. </b>

34
00:02:52.291 --> 00:02:55.041
<b>Then there are those who believe</b>

35
00:02:55.041 --> 00:03:06.291
<b>decisions should be made by completely darkening</b>
<b>emotions based purely and solely on facts.</b>

36
00:03:06.291 --> 00:03:08.791
<b>So what's right?</b>

37
00:03:08.791 --> 00:03:17.166
<b>If decisions are made purely emotionally, </b>
<b>there's a risk of error, just like Arjuna.</b>

38
00:03:17.166 --> 00:03:18.750
<b>Yet</b>

39
00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:27.583
<b>decisions cannot be made by completely</b>
<b> ignoring emotions and considering only facts.</b>

40
00:03:27.583 --> 00:03:35.708
<b>After all, your decisions affect others too.</b>

41
00:03:35.708 --> 00:03:42.208
<b>It's essential that when choosing any path, </b>
<b>we understand the facts,</b>

42
00:03:42.208 --> 00:03:49.958
<b>while also comprehending how our </b>
<b>decision impacts everyone involved.</b>

43
00:03:49.958 --> 00:03:53.250
<b>Weighing both emotions and facts, </b>

44
00:03:53.250 --> 00:04:00.833
<b>finding their harmony that's the right way to </b>
<b>make any major decision, to choose any path.</b>

45
00:04:04.833 --> 00:04:09.000
<b>Here, if in this state of such deep anxiety,</b>

46
00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.958
<b>in this grave dilemma,</b>

47
00:04:11.958 --> 00:04:18.500
<b>without making Arjuna aware of the various </b>
<b>options and their different consequences, </b>

48
00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:22.541
<b>if I were to just give him a two-word command,</b>

49
00:04:22.541 --> 00:04:25.500
<b>saying 'fight now.'</b>

50
00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:30.166
<b>Then would he embrace this decision?</b>

51
00:04:30.166 --> 00:04:38.208
<b>Would he fight with his full capability?</b>

52
00:04:38.208 --> 00:04:44.333
<b>Imposed commands never prove effective.</b>

53
00:04:44.333 --> 00:04:48.291
<b>In family life, when someone</b>
<b>younger faces a dilemma</b>

54
00:04:48.291 --> 00:04:51.041
<b>should I do this or that?</b>

55
00:04:51.041 --> 00:04:55.750
<b>When they seek your opinion</b>
<b>about certain choices,</b>

56
00:04:55.750 --> 00:05:00.125
<b>how do you help?</b>

57
00:05:00.125 --> 00:05:05.625
<b>Sometimes we feel it's best to </b>
<b>just tell them the right option,</b>

58
00:05:05.625 --> 00:05:08.166
<b>to simply give directions.</b>

59
00:05:08.166 --> 00:05:10.958
<b>After all, you're experienced,</b>

60
00:05:10.958 --> 00:05:15.750
<b>completely confident in your guidance.</b>

61
00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:18.625
<b>But think about it</b>

62
00:05:18.625 --> 00:05:23.958
<b>this isn't really about right or wrong.</b>

63
00:05:23.958 --> 00:05:25.750
<b>Consider,</b>

64
00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:28.708
<b>which help is better?</b>

65
00:05:28.708 --> 00:05:33.666
<b>When you merely point out the right path</b>

66
00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:37.500
<b>or when you explain the options,</b>

67
00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:40.125
<b>analyze their consequences,</b>

68
00:05:40.125 --> 00:05:40.791
<b>and</b>

69
00:05:40.791 --> 00:05:49.375
<b>then share which option you </b>
<b>think is right, and why?</b>

70
00:05:49.375 --> 00:05:51.208
<b>What's better?</b>

71
00:05:51.208 --> 00:05:53.750
<b>Just showing the right path?</b>

72
00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:54.541
<b>Or</b>

73
00:05:54.541 --> 00:06:01.708
<b>teaching them how to choose </b>
<b>the right path alongside?</b>

74
00:06:01.708 --> 00:06:03.958
<b>Don't just give directions</b>

75
00:06:03.958 --> 00:06:08.375
<b>explain your experienced thinking </b>
<b>completely, teach them.</b>

76
00:06:08.375 --> 00:06:10.375
<b>That's</b>

77
00:06:10.375 --> 00:06:12.333
<b>true help.</b>

78
00:06:16.666 --> 00:06:20.041
<b>Arjuna has sought my help,</b>

79
00:06:20.041 --> 00:06:24.041
<b>requested guidance for the right path.</b>

80
00:06:24.041 --> 00:06:26.250
<b>And I want him</b>

81
00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:29.125
<b>not only to choose the right path</b>

82
00:06:29.125 --> 00:06:35.166
<b>but also to fully understand </b>
<b>the wisdom behind it.</b>

83
00:06:35.166 --> 00:06:37.458
<b>To know dharma and duty,</b>

84
00:06:37.458 --> 00:06:39.375
<b>recognize the soul,</b>

85
00:06:39.375 --> 00:06:43.166
<b>and understand virtue and sin.</b>

86
00:06:43.166 --> 00:06:46.208
<b>This way, not just today</b>

87
00:06:46.208 --> 00:06:49.958
<b>but lifelong, even in the most </b>
<b>challenging circumstances,</b>

88
00:06:49.958 --> 00:06:54.250
<b>he'll be capable of choosing </b>
<b>the right path independently,</b>

89
00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:58.291
<b>Understanding this one process of path selection,</b>

90
00:06:58.291 --> 00:07:04.875
<b>no life situation will seem</b>
<b>difficult to him anymore.</b>

91
00:07:04.875 --> 00:07:10.166
<b>Here are two professional life lessons to learn.</b>

92
00:07:10.166 --> 00:07:12.250
<b>First</b>

93
00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:16.083
<b>When you're in a serious predicament,</b>

94
00:07:16.083 --> 00:07:18.333
<b>don't panic.</b>

95
00:07:18.333 --> 00:07:21.458
<b>There are many people in your life</b>

96
00:07:21.458 --> 00:07:27.875
<b>who have seen, solved, and learned</b>
<b>from such predicaments.</b>

97
00:07:27.875 --> 00:07:30.083
<b>Benefit from their experience.</b>

98
00:07:30.083 --> 00:07:32.500
<b>Seek their counsel.</b>

99
00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:35.333
<b>Second</b>

100
00:07:35.333 --> 00:07:38.875
<b>If someone comes to you with a predicament,</b>

101
00:07:38.875 --> 00:07:42.541
<b>don't just show them the right path</b>

102
00:07:42.541 --> 00:07:45.083
<b>share your experience,</b>

103
00:07:45.083 --> 00:07:49.666
<b>explain your process of choosing options.</b>

104
00:07:49.666 --> 00:07:53.916
<b>Teaching them is the real help they need.</b>

105
00:07:53.916 --> 00:07:55.708
<b>Think about it</b>

106
00:07:55.708 --> 00:07:59.291
<b>how wonderful would a workplace be</b>

107
00:07:59.291 --> 00:08:04.500
<b>where people don't hesitate to seek counsel,</b>

108
00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:10.791
<b>and readily help others with their experience.</b>

